[#:seon.task{:name "task-creation-is-not-an-agent-call"
             :plan "my.task (the agent-facing API) exposes `my.task/current` and `my.task/send-back!` but not task creation or refinement: `seon.task/create!` upserts a runtime task from a declaration, yet (dir my.task) does not list a call over it, so an agent cannot file a finding as a task or edit its own task. Done when `my.task/update!` over `seon.task/create!`'s upsert, with the agent's world supplied, is listed by (dir my.task), documented with an example, and a regression edits a task from an agent's evaluation (plan §0 item 6)."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-send-back-stores-its-counterexample-for-the-next-attempts-agent"
             :plan "`my.task/send-back!` accepts `:my.task/counterexample` and returns it in its reply, but no attribute stores it: `seon.turn/end-task-call` writes the reason and target on the sending attempt, and `seon.context/send-backs` (the `:seon.context/send-backs` block of `my.task/current` and the current-state block) renders only the reason, so the next attempt's agent never sees the counterexample (step-context lane). Declare the counterexample as a Malli-schemed attribute on the sending attempt, written by `seon.turn/end-task-call` in the same transaction as the reason, and have `seon.context/send-backs` carry it as data beside the reason. Proof: the `my.task-test` deftest `a-send-back-with-a-counterexample-shows-it-to-the-next-attempt` the implementer writes first sends back with `{:expected 1 :actual 2}`, launches the target's next attempt and asserts `(:seon.context/send-backs (my.task/current))` holds that map."}
 #:seon.task{:name "reading-the-current-task-mid-attempt-costs-gigabytes"
             :plan "Live run 13 (`docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-19/live-run-13.md`), Design and Prove attempts on default at 4313acf79: single forms reading `my.task/current` cost 1.4 to 4.3 s and 1.8 to 3.7 GB, against 69 ms and 90 MB for the same read at the attempt's start. Forms (attempt, form): a Design's `my.task/update!` of its own plan, `(get-in (my.task/current) [:seon.context/task :seon.task/sym])` as the task, 4,266 ms 3,682 MB (c9faebbf6e29, 24); `(def next-task (get-in (my.task/current) [:seon.context/chain :seon.context/after 0 :seon.task/sym]))` 1,618 ms 2,276 MB (4bec20fc6ff4, 28); the Prove template's own `my.task/update!` of the next task's proofs 1,445 ms 1,845 MB (4bec20fc6ff4, 31); a `let` pulling the current task and its next one 1,768 ms 2,623 MB (fc99cdd864e6, 48). Each came after the agent had defined a deftest or run a check on its branch. Measure one of them with `seon.profile/measure` on a kept branch (`:chain-16572b11dd32`, `:chain-6097a5caea6f`), name the instrumented functions responsible, and fix that producer; related: `seon.context/one-agents-current-state-costs-hundreds-of-megabytes`."}
]
